/* book exam traps: Adding a dBm value to a dB value. PT, PR and the received power are in dBm; the losses and the margin are in dB. | Leaving the margin out of the used total, or putting it into the received power. The received power counts physical losses only; the margin is held back from the spare. | Miscounting joints: 60 km in 10 km reels has five splices, not six, and both end connectors count. | Treating sensitivity as the only limit. A short link with a strong laser can exceed the overload level and fail from too much light. | Leaving out the dispersion power penalty when the link is close to its dispersion limit. */
